.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt WORDPROCESS-CONFIG 5
.Os WordProcess 1.0
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wordprocess-config
.Nd WordProcess configuration files and settings
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
WordProcess separates machine-wide user preferences from settings stored in a
native document set.
On Unix, its configuration root is
.Pa ~/.wordprocess .
.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.wordprocess/user.dictionary
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/startup.lua
Trusted Lua code executed after core initialisation and before the interactive
screen starts.
Override for one invocation with
.Fl -config .
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/settings.dat
Serialised global settings.
Do not edit it as text.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/templates/
Default template directory.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/templates/default.wp
Loaded for new document sets when its native format matches the application.
.It Pa ~/.wordprocess/user.dictionary
Words accepted by the user spellchecker.
.El
.
.Sh GLOBAL SETTINGS
Global settings include editor width and wrapping, display theme, scrolling,
Tab behaviour, paragraph presentation, GUI dimensions and fonts, template and
autosave directories, system dictionary, recent files, and debug status terms.
.
.Sh DOCUMENT-SET SETTINGS
The native set stores autosave, scrapbook, smart-quote, spellchecker, HTML
export, clipboard, and status-bar settings.
Each document stores its content, cursor, margin view, and physical page layout;
that layout determines the independent physical page status field.
.
.Sh AUTOSAVE
Autosave is disabled by default and requires one prior manual save.
The default interval is ten minutes and the default filename pattern is
.Dq %F.autosave.%T.wp .
.Sy %F
is the primary base filename and
.Sy %T
is a timestamp.
An explicit global autosave directory overrides the primary file's directory.
.
.Sh STARTUP SCRIPTING
The startup file may call high-level functions in the
.Sy Cmd
table, register callbacks with
.Fn AddEventListener ,
and change bindings with
.Fn OverrideKey .
Scripts run with the user's process permissions and are not sandboxed.
The low-level
.Sy wg
Lua table is an internal native bridge retained for source compatibility; it is
unrelated to the native filename extension.
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wp 1 ,
.Xr xwp 1 ,
.Xr wordprocess 5
